speechtext:
I did not quite realize, Mr. Chairman, when you made your proposal what was actually intended. What we are really doing now is treating all these amendments as incorporated and taking this as a new bill. On page 10, clause 19, I notice there is an amendment which makes the paragraph read as follows:
(h) the amount of discounts or loans that may be made to directors, either jointly or severally, or to any one person, or to any shareholders;
That apparently is an amendment and I would like to have the significance of that explained by the minister.
